Package: rkzc
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: eunkyo3 <eunkyo3@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: video
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @SHLIBS_DEPENDS@, wget, ca-certificates
Recommends: python3
Suggests: netcat-openbsd
Homepage: https://github.com/eunkyo3/rk3588s-zero-copy
Description: object detection on RTSP streams with RK3588's zero-copy path
 Hardware decode (MPP), letterbox on the RGA and inference on the NPU of an
 RK3588 board, with no CPU copy of the pixels between them.
 .
 The package holds the program rkzc-detect with its systemd service (a
 configuration file in, JSON lines out), the library librkzc with its C++, C
 and Python interfaces, and ffmpeg-rockchip's libraries (LGPL v3) in
 /opt/rkzc/lib.
 .
 Rockchip's NPU runtime librknnrt is downloaded from Rockchip at install; a
 model is fetched by the separate command rkzc-fetch-model. Neither is in the
 package. Tested on a NanoPi R6C with FriendlyElec's Ubuntu 24.04 image.
